important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn9le12ob08re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le12ob08re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn9le12ob08re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn9le12ob08re2img01.jpg", "text": "Yesterday afternoon, I received a frantic telephone call from my best friend, Rebecca, who had worked the graveyard shift for the last three months. She sounded very annoyed and in desperate need of some peace and quiet. She was suffering from a terrible headache and was frustrated that she had to deal with inconsiderate neighbors. It was so noisy around there that she had even bought earplugs and taken a sleeping tablet.", "id": 1}, {"time": "25000", "image": "engenn9le12ob08re2img02.jpg", "text": "The baby next door had been crying for hours and she couldn't fathom why the child's parents hadn't done anything about it. The little boy across the hall had practiced his electric guitar every day this week despite complaints from other tenants.The neighbors across the hall were arguing as usual. They had been arguing since the day they moved in. Just to make things worse, the man upstairs was pacing nonstop and moving the furniture. She said she had to get out of here and was coming right over. I was delighted to have Rebecca as a visitor, and rushed out to buy something at the bakery.", "id": 2}, {"time": "62900", "image": "engenn9le12ob08re2img03.jpg", "text": "However, I wished she hadn't hung up so quickly. She didn't give me time to tell her that the road in front of my house has been under repair for weeks! There were maintenance crews everywhere, and the asphalt was being relaid. She wasn't going to get any sleep at my house either. She ended up falling asleep in front of the television. Poor girl!", "id": 3}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "5000", "image": "", "text": "Writing a diary entry.", "id": 1}, {"time": "15500", "image": "", "text": "<span class=\"bullet\">Parts of a diary entry.</span>", "id": 2}], "video_src": "engenn9le12ob08re3vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "video", "id": 2, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Anecdotes and Personal Stories"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": " No Peace and Quiet"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le12ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect tense vs. Past Simple tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way. <br/>You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> necessarily connected to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about experience.<br/>When you use the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "To help you decide whether you should use the Present Perfect tense or the Past Simple tense, ask yourself the questions \u2018When?'"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you can answer the question \u2018When?', the past time is stated or inferred or understood. Use the Past Simple. There is no connection to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you cannot answer the question \u2018When?', because the time is not stated or not important, then choose the Present Perfect tense. There is instead a connection to the present."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Sentence\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">When she called, she told me about her situation. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" when she called\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> She's just arrived at my house.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"  from the time she left  to now\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Yesterday afternoon, I received a frantic telephone call from my best friend."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The road in front of my house has been under repair for weeks! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She has worked the graveyard shift at the hospital for the last three months. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Past Continuous tense v.s Past Simple tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Past Continuous tense to talk about an action that was happening at a time before now. <br/>You use the Simple Past to talk about a finished past action. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the Past Continuous to: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>to describe the background in a story written in the past tense </li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">My friend <span class=\"strong\">was watching</span> television."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>to describe an action that was interrupted by another event or action</li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">While <span class=\"strong\">she was</span> watching television there was a knock at the door.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The form of the Past Continuous is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">was/were</span> + verb-<span class=\"italic\">ing</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "She was suffering from a terrible headache and was frustrated that she had to deal with inconsiderate neighbors. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I received a frantic telephone call from my best friend, Rebecca."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The man upstairs was pacing nonstop and moving the furniture. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Simple Past to talk about a shorter action or event that happened in the middle of, or interrupted, the longer action."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">They were taking turns, swapping stories , and helping each other when her husband <span class=\"strong\">arrived</span>.</span>"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you talk about the experiences of a friend."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fathom"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to understand "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She couldn't fathom why the child's parents hadn't done anything about it. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "graveyard shift"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a work shift which is during  late night and early morning hours"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Rebecca has worked the graveyard shift for the last three months."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "inconsiderate "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not caring about other people's feelings"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She  was frustrated that she had to deal with inconsiderate neighbors."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "electric guitar"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a guitar whose tone is magnified electrically by a microphone or pick-up device"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The little boy across the hall had practiced his electric guitar every day this week."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "asphalt"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a black substance that forms a hard surface when it dries; it is commonly used as a surface for roads"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The asphalt was being relaid."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pace"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to walk in one direction and then in the opposite direction, repeatedly "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The man upstairs was pacing nonstop and moving the furniture."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob08aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tenant "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a person who rents a room, building, or piece of land"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Despite complaints from other tenants, the boy played his electric guitar all the week."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le12ob08aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a 120-150 word diary entry about a time when a friend helped you in a difficult situation. What happened?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe the situation.  Answer the questions who, what, when, where and why."}, {"type": "text", "content": "What was your reaction? How did you feel?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "How did they assist you?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "What happened in the end?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the Past Continuous tense and the Simple Past tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When completed, read the diary entry aloud to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a diary entry about a personal experience."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe my reactions in certain events."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about the past using a range of grammatical forms in a diary entry."}]}]}